==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Devil Egg: N006''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Fallen Bear Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, it may be used as an emergency meatshield in [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] if you have no use for its True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
Much like [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Teacher BearCat]] against his target traits in various forms, this unit's devastating potential is held back by short range and lack of defensive abilities (namely [[Surge Attack|Surge]] immunity) to compensate, nor can it pierce [[Shield]]s. While being a spammable, low-cost unit does alleviate these risks somewhat, they cannot be ignored, as it limits Fallen Bear Cat mostly to common Aku threats that have lower range or slow attack rates, such as [[Aku Doge]], [[Sinner Snache]], [[Cerberus Kids]], [[Aku Gory]], [[Le'Behemoth]], [[Wicked Face]], [[Miz Devil]], [[Devil Wife]] and to a lesser extent [[Condemned Peng]], although most of these matchups can be risky at times. Aku Gory is its most valuable target overall, but the range difference is only 5, so Aku Gory is bound to hit Fallen Bear Cat if he moves forward even a little.

Fallen Bear Cat also has Behemoth Slayer, although it is only really worthwhile against [[Wild Doge]] and [[THE FOLIVOREAN]]. It outranges Wild Doge and has enough damage to instantly knockback a 200% Wild Doge at level 49 (which even [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] cannot do without [[Cat Combo|Combos]]). THE FOLIVOREAN is an Aku Behemoth with a relatively long attack cycle and a weak Shield that regenerates only once, allowing this unit to potentially sneak in a few hits. Starting at level 48, Fallen Bear Cat even has enough health to survive a hit from a 200% FOLIVOREAN. Fallen Bear Cat can also land the occasional hit on an unprotected [[Vermilingua Rangmaster]], but is far from the most reliable option against him and most other [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoths]], since their range and DPS are generally way too much for it to handle.

It's also noteworthy to mention that Fallen Bear Cat has the most expensive cost to evolve out of all the [[Ancient Eggs]], just right behind [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ancient Egg: N000]], so unless you are in desperate need of anti-Aku or anti-Behemoth units and have no better options, do not invest in this unit.

